The distinction is elementary but essential. A snapshot of an electron distribution is a configuration; it is not yet an orbit. If space is replaced by a lattice and time by a sequence $t_0,t_1,t_2,\ldots$, then motion is the succession $\ket{s(t_0)}
  \longmapsto
  \ket{s(t_1)}
  \longmapsto
  \ket{s(t_2)}
  \longmapsto\cdots.$ A physical model therefore needs both a set of possible states and an update rule.

