Fundamental classical dynamics does not permit this loss when every degree of freedom is retained. The required property has two halves: $\boxed{\begin{gathered}
    \text{one unique future and one unique past}\\
    \text{for every state}
  \end{gathered}.}$ For a finite state space, the update must therefore be a permutation. Every state has exactly one outgoing arrow and exactly one incoming arrow, so the diagram decomposes into disjoint cycles.

