To calculate $A'=MA$, take the inner product of each row of $M$ with the input column: $A'_i=(MA)_i=\sum_{j=1}^{4}M_{ij}A_j.$ For example, $\begin{aligned}
  A'_1&=M_{11}A_1+M_{12}A_2+M_{13}A_3+M_{14}A_4,\\
  A'_2&=M_{21}A_1+M_{22}A_2+M_{23}A_3+M_{24}A_4.\end{aligned}$ The third and fourth entries follow by the same pattern.

